<abstract>
<para>
&i18n-kapplication; is a chat client for AI language models.
</para>
</abstract>

<keywordset>
<keyword>KDE</keyword>
<keyword>AI</keyword>
<keyword>chat</keyword>
<keyword>Ollama</keyword>
<keyword>LLM</keyword>
</keywordset>
</bookinfo>

<chapter id="introduction">
<title>Introduction</title>

<para>&i18n-kapplication; is a chat application that lets you talk with AI language
models, either running locally with Ollama or provided by an online AI service.</para>

<para>Conversations are stored in a local database on your computer, so they are
still there the next time you start the application. You can browse them, search
through them, archive the ones you do not need any more, and export them to a file.</para>

<para>&i18n-kapplication; does not provide a model of its own: it talks to a model
provider that you configure. Nothing is sent anywhere until you have set up such a
provider and asked a question.</para>

</chapter>

<chapter id="getting-started">
<title>Getting Started</title>

<para>Before you can ask anything, &i18n-kapplication; needs at least one
<emphasis>instance</emphasis>. An instance is a configured connection to a model
provider: a local server running on your own machine, or an online service.</para>

<para>The first time you start the application without any instance, it offers to
create one. You can also open
<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure
&i18n-kapplication;…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and go to the
<guilabel>Instances</guilabel> page.</para>

<sect1 id="local-model">
<title>Using a local model</title>

<para>Running the model on your own computer keeps your questions on your machine.
&i18n-kapplication; can use local servers such as
<application>Ollama</application>, <application>llama.cpp</application> or
<application>LM Studio</application>.</para>

<para>Install and start the server first, then add an instance of the matching type.
The default address of a local <application>Ollama</application> server is already
filled in. If <application>Ollama</application> is installed but not running,
&i18n-kapplication; offers to start it for you; you can also do this from the command
line with <userinput><command>kaichat</command>
<option>--start-ollama</option></userinput>.</para>

<para>Once the instance is connected you still need a model. Models can be
downloaded from within the instance configuration, and &i18n-kapplication; notifies
you when a download is finished.</para>

</sect1>

<sect1 id="online-service">
<title>Using an online service</title>

<para>&i18n-kapplication; can also talk to hosted services, among them
Ollama Cloud, OpenAI, Anthropic, Mistral AI, Groq, Grok, Qwen, OpenRouter,
DeepInfra, Novita AI, Cerebras and other providers with an OpenAI-compatible
interface. The exact list depends on the plugins installed on your system; run
<userinput><command>kaichat</command> <option>--plugin-info</option></userinput> to
see it.</para>

<para>Create an instance of the matching type and paste the API key given to you by
the service. Be aware that with an online service your questions, and any file you
attach, are sent to that provider and are subject to its own privacy policy.</para>

</sect1>

</chapter>

<chapter id="using-kapp">
<title>Using &i18n-kapplication;</title>

<sect1 id="main-window">
<title>The main window</title>

<para>The window is split in three parts:</para>

<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>the list of your chats, on the left. It can be collapsed with the
button on the splitter;</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>the conversation itself, on the right, where your questions and the
answers of the model are shown;</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>the input field at the bottom, where you type your
question.</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>

<para>Above them, a header bar lets you start a new chat and search in the current
conversation. The status bar at the bottom shows what the model is currently doing,
for instance which tool it is calling.</para>

</sect1>

<sect1 id="chatting">
<title>Asking questions</title>

<para>Type your question in the input field and validate it. The answer appears in
the conversation view as it is being generated, and a notification is shown when a
long answer is finished.</para>

<para>You can attach files to a question, and enable the tools the model is allowed
to call while answering it. Each chat keeps its own history, which is sent along
with your new question so that the model knows the context.</para>

</sect1>

<sect1 id="managing-chats">
<title>Managing chats</title>

<para>Chats are created from the header bar, or with
<userinput><command>kaichat</command> <option>--new-chat</option>
<replaceable>title</replaceable></userinput>.</para>

<para>A chat you do not need any more can be archived instead of being deleted.
Archived chats are hidden from the list; show them again with
<menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show
Archive</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.</para>

<para>To look for something you asked or read some time ago, use
<menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Search in Database…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.
This searches the whole stored history, not only the chat you are looking at. The
number of matches is shown in the status bar.</para>

</sect1>

<sect1 id="quick-ask">
<title>Quick Ask</title>

<para>Quick Ask is a small dialog for a single question, without opening the main
window. Open it with
<menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Open Quick
Ask…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, with the
<keycombo action="simul">&Meta;<keycap>Space</keycap></keycombo> global shortcut, or
with <userinput><command>kaichat</command> <option>--quick-ask</option></userinput>.
Questions asked this way are not added to your chats.</para>

</sect1>

<sect1 id="import-export">
<title>Importing and exporting chats</title>

<para>The current chat can be saved to a file with
<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Export…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>,
in one of four formats:</para>

<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><guimenuitem>Export as JSON…</guimenuitem></term>
<listitem><para>A <filename class="extension">.kaichat</filename> file. This is the
only format that &i18n-kapplication; can read back.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guimenuitem>Export as Markdown…</guimenuitem></term>
<listitem><para>A text file keeping the formatting of the answers.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guimenuitem>Export as Text…</guimenuitem></term>
<listitem><para>Plain text.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guimenuitem>Export as Pdf…</guimenuitem></term>
<listitem><para>A printable document.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>

<para>A previously exported <filename class="extension">.kaichat</filename> file is
read back with
<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Import…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.
You can also open such a file from your file manager, or pass it on the command
line.</para>

</sect1>

<sect1 id="appearance">
<title>Adjusting the display</title>

<para>The text of the whole application can be made bigger or smaller with
<menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guisubmenu>Font Size</guisubmenu></menuchoice>,
or with <keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>+</keycap></keycombo> and
<keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>-</keycap></keycombo>. A fixed font can be
chosen in the configuration dialog instead.</para>

<para><menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guisubmenu>Color
Scheme</guisubmenu></menuchoice> switches the colors of the window without changing
your desktop settings, and <keycap>F11</keycap> switches to full screen.</para>

<para>The menu bar can be hidden with
<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show
Menubar</guimenuitem></menuchoice>; the actions stay available through the hamburger
button of the toolbar.</para>

</sect1>

</chapter>

<chapter id="configuring">
<title>Configuring &i18n-kapplication;</title>

<para>The configuration dialog is opened with
<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure
&i18n-kapplication;…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Depending on how the application was
built, it has the following pages.</para>

<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>General</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Whether the system tray icon is shown, and the system prompt sent to
the model at the beginning of every conversation.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Font</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Use a font of your choice instead of the system one.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Instances</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Add, remove and configure the connections to your model providers,
and manage the models available on them.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>MCP Servers</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Model Context Protocol servers, which give the model access to
external data and actions. This support is still experimental.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Spell Checking</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Spell checking of what you type.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Accessibility</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Text-to-speech settings, when the application was built with
text-to-speech support.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Plugins</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Enable or disable the installed plugins and configure the tools the
model may use.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>User Feedback</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>How much information, if any, you want to send to the developers.
Nothing is sent unless you ask for it here.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>

<para>Notifications are configured with
<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure
Notifications…</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.</para>

<para>Instances and MCP servers can also be configured outside of the application,
from the <guilabel>AI</guilabel> module of &systemsettings;.</para>

<sect1 id="files">
<title>Files used</title>

<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><filename>~/.config/kaichatrc</filename></term>
<listitem><para>The settings of the application.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><filename class="directory">~/.local/share/kaichat/ai-database/</filename></term>
<listitem><para>The databases holding your chats and their messages.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>

<para>The configuration of your instances contains the API keys of the online
services you use. Treat these files as you would treat a password.</para>

</sect1>

</chapter>

<chapter id="command-line">
<title>Command Line Options</title>

<para>&i18n-kapplication; runs as a single instance: starting it again while it is
already running passes the options to the window that is already open instead of
opening a second one.</para>

<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>--list-instances</option></term>
<listitem><para>Print the configured instances and exit.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>--list-chats</option></term>
<listitem><para>Print the titles of the stored chats and exit.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>--plugin-info</option></term>
<listitem><para>Print the available text and tool plugins and exit.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>--instance</option> <replaceable>name</replaceable></term>
<listitem><para>Start with a specific instance.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>--new-chat</option> <replaceable>title</replaceable></term>
<listitem><para>Create a new chat with this title.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>--switch-to-chat</option> <replaceable>name</replaceable></term>
<listitem><para>Switch to an existing chat, by title.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>--switch-to-chat-from-id</option> <replaceable>id</replaceable></term>
<listitem><para>Switch to an existing chat, by identifier.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>--ask-message</option> <replaceable>message</replaceable></term>
<listitem><para>Ask this question straight away.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>--attach</option> <replaceable>url</replaceable></term>
<listitem><para>Attach a file to the question. Can be repeated.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>--tool</option> <replaceable>name</replaceable></term>
<listitem><para>Allow the model to use this tool. Can be repeated.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>--quick-ask</option></term>
<listitem><para>Open the Quick Ask dialog.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>--import</option> <replaceable>file</replaceable></term>
<listitem><para>Import a chat from a JSON file.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>--start-ollama</option></term>
<listitem><para>Start the local <application>Ollama</application> program.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>--debug</option></term>
<listitem><para>Enable debug mode, which adds a <guimenu>Debug</guimenu> menu
showing the content of the database.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>--feedback</option></term>
<listitem><para>List the information that can be sent as user feedback.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><replaceable>file…</replaceable></term>
<listitem><para>Chat files to import.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>

<para>On systems with &DBus;, a running &i18n-kapplication; also exposes the
<interfacename>org.kde.kaichat.Application</interfacename> interface, which offers
the same operations as the options above: listing chats, creating one, switching to
one, showing archived chats and asking a question.</para>

</chapter>

